WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.940
The media's always looking for something to
blame.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.860
In part it's motivated by a political desire
to find a group that isn't politically active

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.749
or politically powerful

00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:11.749
as a scapegoat.

00:00:11.749 --> 00:00:16.300
The Department of Justice is at the Phillips
house taking all their ammunition and their guns.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:22.220
So they have my guns outside, taking pictures
of it where the neighbors are driving by.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:31.200
In the wake of mass shootings, our media and
our politicians tend to focus on two things:

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.120
banning certain kinds of weapons

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.500
and keeping weapons out of the hands of certain
kinds of people.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.860
None of us want crazy people having guns,
look what happened.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:44.020
I'm afraid that that semi-automatic weapon
is going to fall in tot he hands of a crazy person.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:47.300
A dozen more killers, a hundred more?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:57.220
How can we possibly even guess how many given
our nation's refusal

00:00:57.220 --> 00:01:03.160
to create an active national database of the
mentally ill.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:07.360
That's Wayne LaPierre, head spokesperson for
the National Rifle Association.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:12.780
An active national database of the mentally
ill.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.040
Even the nation's premiere gun lobby believes
that a database

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.700
to keep guns away from the mentally ill seems
like a good idea.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.080
Better safe than sorry, it seems, well, logical.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.100
But what if there's a serious flaw in that
logic.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:28.980
There is no evidence that the mentally ill

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:34.380
account for a largely disproportionate amount
of violence or gun violence.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.060
Here's the entire population of people with
a mental illness diagnosis

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.970
and when you control for the complicating
factor of substance abuse

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.200
here's the number of them statistically likely
to commit a violent act.

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.020
Only about four percent.

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:50.640
General strategies that forensic psychiatrists
take

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:57.380
is that one never attempts to predict violence
in a large pool of un-selected individuals.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:03.820
If you have a test that is 90% accurate and
you applied it to a hundred thousand people

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:09.240
the rate of violence is roughly half a percent
in the general population.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.980
So there are five hundred real violent people,

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:16.560
but you've identified ten thousand people
inappropriately as being violent.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.920
In the absence of a history of violence or
any other risk factors

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.780
it is impossible to identify who will go on
to become violent.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:29.060
For every individual who goes on a shooting
rampage

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:31.840
there are a hundred or perhaps more individuals

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:38.020
who also had disturbed relationships with
teachers, parents.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:42.880
Authorities want to know what caused the alleged
gunman Jared Lee Loughner to snap.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.540
We hear it over and over again.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.560
If he'd been transported to a psych ward,
the shootings might never have happened.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.220
There were clear warning signs.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.060
Here to talk about the warning signs in a
case like this-

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:54.940
Should we have been picking up some signs
on this guy-

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.400
-we should be looking for in an individual
like this?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:02.660
Once we know the outcome, it is easy to look
back and perceive a pattern

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.860
that seems to be leading to a common event.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.080
Often that's simply hindsight bias.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:14.400
If we put doctors in a position of acting
on behalf of the government

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:18.879
or acting on behalf of social control.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.660
Then that undermines the therapeutic mission.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.739
Restricting the rights to people who are living
with a mental illness

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.519
or possibly maybe diagnosed with a mental
illness

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:30.720
just further perpetuates people not receiving
or seeking

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.000
the treatment that they need to get better

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.140
and we know prevention, early intervention
and seeking that treatment right on the onset

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.880
is what supports people in recovery.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:45.560
So most people with mental illnesses never
do anything violent

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:51.600
and it's almost impossible to predict who's
going to snap without a prior history of violence.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.020
But still, what's the harm in taking precautions?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.960
To answer that question, we turn to California.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:04.400
California's Armed Prohibited Persons System
aims to confiscate guns from three groups:

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.480
Those with a history of violence.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.060
Wanted criminals.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:12.040
And anyone the state believes has a severe
mental illness.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:19.199
Because one nurse wrote false information,
now I'm on a prohibited persons list.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.180
I've never done anything to hurt anybody.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.160
Lynette Phillips and her husband David have
never committed a violent crime

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:27.940
and Lynette is certainly not a wanted felon.

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.920
But she does have a mental illness.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:33.980
I was diagnosed about 13 years ago with anxiety
disorder.

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:36.719
Once I was diagnosed I felt

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.100
'okay this makes sense now, this excessive
worrying.'

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:46.700
And once the medication started taking effect,
I felt like a normal person.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.580
Lynette ran into trouble when she switched
her medication from a pill to a patch.

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.700
She rushed the transition because she wanted
to be well in time for her first Christmas

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.220
with a new grand daughter.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:05.440
What ended up happening was I couldn't stop
crying and there wasn't anything I saw, experienced,

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.800
everything would make me cry.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.220
Desperate to stop crying, Lynette asked her
son to find a hospital for her to check herself into

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.240
so she could stabilize her mood.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:19.580
The local hospital was full so they ended
up at a facility called Aurora Charter Oak.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:24.620
That's where my nightmare started, I thought
my nightmare crying was-

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.000
That was a piece of cake.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.820
I was admitted based on me being suicidal,
that I could potentially drive my car off a cliff.

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:36.840
Which I never said those words, the nurse
never said those words.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:40.960
So where the cliff came in to play, I don't
know.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.820
Once I said goodbye to my husband, once I
got to the unit,

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.940
they did their assessment and started giving
me paperwork

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:55.200
and that's when I realized I was being, I
was 5150, involuntarily being admitted.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:06:00.960
Despite voluntarily seeking treatment, Lynette
was involuntarily committed to the hospital.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.260
Representatives at Aurora Charter Oak declined
to comment for this story.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:09.500
But Lynette says she was released before the
full 72 hours,

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.420
once the hospital psychiatrist actually had
a chance to see her.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:18.580
He said better policies and procedures should
be in effect so this doesn't happen.

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:23.000
Nobody apologized, that's closest to an apology
as I got.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:25.980
Lynette has a letter from her personal psychiatrist

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.880
backing up her claim that she sought treatment
voluntarily.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:35.620
But because of the involuntary commitment,
she suddenly became an armed prohibited person.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:39.819
California Department of Justice officers
showed up with no warrant

00:06:39.819 --> 00:06:41.979
and took every gun in the house.

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:45.500
I don't even know what gun it was I bought
for Dave for Christmas.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.320
Couldn't have told you.

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:48.440
Never loaded a gun.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:53.520
You bring nine officers to the house, you
surround the house, how much is that costing?

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:58.100
They didn't need to do that, they embarrassed
us in the neighborhood.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:02.000
It is humiliating when someone comes to your
door and treats you like a criminal.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.900
It's not how we should be treating people
who are living with an illness.

00:07:05.909 --> 00:07:09.580
To the extent that society continues to vilify
the mentally ill

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:13.940
and to scapegoat them as being the primary
cause of gun violence

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:15.920
is a major step backward.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:22.640
There needs to be some better policing of
who they're coming after.

